public class MultipleCatchFlowDemo {
    public static void executeOperation(int scenario) {
        System.out.println("\nExecuting Scenario: " + scenario);
        try {
            if (scenario == 1) {
                int[] arr = {10, 20};
                System.out.println(arr[5]); // ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
            } else if (scenario == 2) {
                int res = 100 / 0; // ArithmeticException
            } else if (scenario == 3) {
                Integer.parseInt("NotANumber"); // NumberFormatException
            } else {
                System.out.println("Clean execution!");
            }
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("-> Block 1: Caught ArithmeticException: " + e.getMessage());
        } catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
            System.out.println("-> Block 2: Caught ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException: " + e.getMessage());
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            System.out.println("-> Block 3: Caught NumberFormatException: " + e.getMessage());
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.out.println("-> Block 4: Fallback Generic Exception: " + e.getClass().getSimpleName());
        } finally {
            System.out.println("-> Finally: Completed scenario teardown");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        executeOperation(1);
        executeOperation(2);
        executeOperation(3);
        executeOperation(4);
    }
}

questions.question:
What will be printed by the following code?
```java
try {
    int[] arr = new int[2];
    arr[5] = 10 / 0;
} catch (ArithmeticException e) {
    System.out.print("A");
} catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
    System.out.print("B");
}
```

What will be printed?
```java
try {
    try {
        int x = 10 / 0;
    } catch (NullPointerException e) {
        System.out.print("Inner");
    }
} catch (ArithmeticException e) {
    System.out.print("Outer");
}
```

